# Best practice only (no patch-first)

**Will standing order.** Do not open with a patch, workaround, or “先堵一下” option when a cleaner end-state exists.

## Required

1. **Recommend one best-practice end-state** — how the concept should be represented after the change (one source of truth, no contradictory UI/metrics).
2. **Analyze / plan headings:** Heading 3 is that end-state only. Do not present “低风险补丁 vs 最佳实践” as equal choices unless Will explicitly asks for a stopgap.
3. **Implement the same end-state** — widen/rename the sole helper or phase input; do **not** ship a parallel optional `foo?: boolean` / `!!foo` / extra OR branch beside the real gate (Will catch: 2026-11-10 guest awaiting).
4. **Reject as the plan or diff:** hide-when-lying badges, extra if/else beside the real formula, second pending/progress calculator, “先改文案再说口径”, copy-nearby then dedupe later, keep-old + forward-only wrapper.
5. **If unsure which design is best:** ask Will to pick among **best-practice** alternatives — never default to the smallest patch.

## Allowed narrow fixes (not “patches”)

- Typo / one-line apply Will already ordered
- Pure lint/format/docs
- Implementing an **already approved** end-state plan

## Conflicts

Wins over “minimal diff”, “ship a small gate first”, and “patch then harden later”. Aligns with `analysis-before-code.mdc` end-state gate and skill `mesa-analyze-before-code`.

## Cross-project

Same standing order is also a **Cursor User Rule** (`Best practice only — never patch-first (all projects)`) so it applies outside this repo.
